<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  THE REVIEWS TAB — Figma 534:9527 (desktop) / 1204:27061 (mobile)
  ===========================================================================
  Two changes, and no restructuring. The block tree Magento_Review declares is
  kept exactly as it is — `reviews.tab` with `product.review.form` beneath it,
  and that form's two extension containers beneath THAT — because the shape of
  that tree is what third-party modules attach to. Magento_ReCaptchaReview, for
  one, injects its widget into `form.additional.review.info`; a flatter tree of
  our own would silently drop the captcha and every review submission would then
  fail server-side validation with nothing on screen to explain it.

  The two TEMPLATES are theme overrides at the same paths core uses
  (templates/review.phtml, templates/form.phtml), so they need no layout
  instruction at all. What follows is the three things that do.

  ===========================================================================
  1. THE VIEW MODEL
  ===========================================================================
  Spartrak\Review\ViewModel\ProductReviews is what the panel prints — the
  average, the two counts and the five bars. Handed to the block as an argument
  rather than reached for inside the template, so the template holds no
  business logic (CLAUDE.md section 8) and the aggregate query has one caller.

  ===========================================================================
  2. THE require-cookie TRIGGER
  ===========================================================================
  Magento_Cookie's `require-cookie` block watches a SELECTOR and warns the
  shopper that their review will not post while cookies are off — the review
  POST needs a form key, and a form key needs a session. Core points it at
  `.review .action.submit`, which are core's own class names on core's own
  review form. This theme's dialog does not carry them, so the notice would
  have quietly stopped working: cookies off, press the button, nothing happens,
  no explanation.

  Repointed at the real submit control rather than adding core's class names to
  Spartrak markup, because the selector is the configuration and the markup is
  the design.

  ===========================================================================
  3. THE DIALOG MOVES OUT OF THE TAB PANEL
  ===========================================================================
  `product.review.form` renders the <dialog>, and it CANNOT stay a child of
  `reviews.tab`, because Magento's tabs widget hides an inactive panel with
  `display: none` — and a <dialog> inside a display:none subtree cannot be
  shown at all. Left in place, the review dialog would work only while the
  reviews tab happened to be the open one, and Magento's own rating summary in
  the product-info column (which links to the review form from the top of the
  page, where the description tab is usually the active one) would open
  nothing.

  MOVED AS A BLOCK, NOT RELOCATED IN JAVASCRIPT. Appending the node to <body>
  on init was the first fix and was rejected: Magento_ReCaptchaReview mounts a
  Knockout component and a Google widget INSIDE this form, and the order of
  `data-mage-init` against `x-magento-init` is not guaranteed — so a DOM move
  can race a captcha that has already mounted. A layout move happens before any
  of it renders, and it keeps the block tree intact, so
  `form.additional.review.info` still resolves and the captcha still lands
  exactly where its own layout file puts it.

  The CTA is unaffected: it lives in review.phtml, inside the panel, where
  Figma draws it.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <move element="product.review.form" destination="content"/>
        <referenceBlock name="reviews.tab">
            <arguments>
                <argument name="view_model" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\Review\ViewModel\ProductReviews</argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>
        <referenceBlock name="require-cookie">
            <arguments>
                <argument name="triggers" xsi:type="array">
                    <item name="submitReviewButton" xsi:type="string">.spartrak-review-dialog__submit</item>
                </argument>
            </arguments>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
